# The visualizer's build junk, ignored HERE rather than in the host repo's
# .gitignore — because this tree travels. A target repo that VENDORS the skill
# (`.agents/skills/…`) has it inside its own working copy, where `up`'s
# first-run `bun install` lands ~50 packages in that repo's `git status`.
# Under `worktree.enabled: false` it is worse than untidy: the commit stage
# stages `run.repo_root`, which is then the main checkout, and `git add -A`
# commits every one of them — a single flag between `just up` and 50 packages
# in the engineer's history. A rule that ships with the directory holds
# wherever the skill is checked out, install.py run or not.
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
